# Input
```svelte
<!-- should generate a diagnostic -->
<script>
let hello = "Hello World";
let written = "Before";
</script>

<div>
    <span>{hello}</span>
    <span>{written = "After"}</span>
</div>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-svelte-template-read.svelte:3:1 lint/style/useConst  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This let declares a variable that is only assigned once.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate a diagnostic -->
    2 │ <script>
  > 3 │ let hello = "Hello World";
      │ ^^^
    4 │ let written = "Before";
    5 │ </script>
  
  i 'hello' is never reassigned.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate a diagnostic -->
    2 │ <script>
  > 3 │ let hello = "Hello World";
      │     ^^^^^
    4 │ let written = "Before";
    5 │ </script>
  
  i A variable that is never reassigned is clearer as const, because it prevents the binding from being reassigned.
  
  i Safe fix: Use const instead.
  
    1 1 │   
    2   │ - let·hello·=·"Hello·World";
      2 │ + const·hello·=·"Hello·World";
    3 3 │   let written = "Before";
    4 4 │   
  

```
